  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $r(x)=|x|\\in D$, because\n\n$$\nr(0)=|0|=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, suppose $f(x),g(x)\\in D,$ where $f(0)=0$ and $g(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nf(0)+g(0)=0+0=0.\n$$\n\nHence $f(x)+g(x)\\in D.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II it true, the set is closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
